## Overview
- You are an expert in Sanity CMS, Sanity Studio, and the entire plugin ecosystem
- You are an expert in creating Sanity schemas and GROQ queries
- Your schemas are always organized and GROQ queries are always performant and optimized

## Common File Paths
| Path | Description |
| :--- | :--- |
| `studio/sanity.config.ts` | Sanity Studio config, plugins, and structure |
| `studio/schemas/schema.ts` | Registers all schema types for Studio |
| `studio/schemas/moduleTypes.ts` | Defines module, relation, and group lists |
| `studio/schemas/common.ts` | Shared reusable fields (title, image, links) |
| `studio/schemas/documents/` | Singleton and standalone document schemas |
| `studio/schemas/pages/` | Page-type schemas (blog, case studies, platform) |
| `studio/schemas/modules/` | Page-builder module block schemas |
| `studio/schemas/objects/` | Reusable object schemas (link, portable-text) |
| `studio/schemas/previews/` | Insert-menu preview images for modules |
| `studio/actions/` | Custom document actions |
| `studio/lib/structure.ts` | Studio desk structure and sidebar grouping |
| `studio/lib/default-document-node.ts` | Default document view configuration |
| `frontend/sanity/queries/queries.ts` | Composes page-level and content-type queries |
| `frontend/sanity/queries/fragments.ts` | Reusable GROQ query fragments |
| `frontend/sanity/queries/functions.ts` | Reusable GROQ function snippets |
| `frontend/sanity/queries/modules/` | Query fragments per module schema |
| `frontend/sanity/queries/documents/` | Query fragments per document schema |
| `frontend/sanity/lib/fetch.ts` | Typed data layer and `ModuleProps` type |
| `frontend/sanity/lib/client.ts` | Sanity client instance configuration |
| `frontend/sanity/lib/live.ts` | `sanityFetch`, live preview, cache setup |
| `frontend/sanity/lib/image.ts` | Image URL builder helper |
| `frontend/sanity.types.ts` | Auto-generated TypeGen output, never edit |
| `frontend/components/modules/ModuleBuilder.tsx` | Maps schema types to React components |
| `plopfile.cjs` | Scaffolds new module component, query, schema, test |

## Schema Authoring
- Always check `studio/schemas/common.ts` for existing reusable fields before defining new ones
- Always write schemas to their own file and export a default matching the filename
- Always add an `icon` from `@sanity/icons` or `lucide-react` to every `document` and `object` type
- Always define a `preview` with contextual `select`/`prepare` for documents and objects
- Always end `description` and validation `error()` copy with a period
- Never write a `boolean` field; use a `string` field with `options.list` instead
- Never write a single `reference` field; always use an `array` of references
- Use `groups` with icons when a schema has more than a few fields
- Use `fieldsets` with `options: { columns: 2 }` for visually related fields (e.g. start/end date)

## New Module Checklist
- Run `pnpm plop` and select `Add New Module` to scaffold component, query, schema, and test files
- Register the schema in `studio/schemas/schema.ts`
- Add the type to `moduleBlocks` (and `moduleGroups`) in `studio/schemas/moduleTypes.ts`
- Add a preview image to `studio/schemas/previews/`
- Add the query fragment to `modulesFragment` in `frontend/sanity/queries/queries.ts`
- Map the component in `frontend/components/modules/ModuleBuilder.tsx`
- Run `pnpm typegen` after any schema or query change

## GROQ Queries
- Always use `defineQuery` from `next-sanity`, imported per project convention
- Always use relative imports inside `frontend/sanity/queries/` — absolute imports break TypeGen
- Always compose page/module queries from fragments in `fragments.ts` and `functions.ts`
- Always annotate manually composed or dynamic queries with `// @sanity-typegen-ignore`
- Never interpolate dynamic values into a query string; always use `$params`

## Naming Conventions
- `studio/schemas/**` and `frontend/sanity/queries/**` files use `kebab-case`
- Schema `name` values must be globally unique across the whole schema
- Query constants use `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` ending in `_QUERY`

## GROQ Rules

Whenever there is an image within a GROQ query, do not expand it unless explicitly instructed to do so.


## GROQ Query Structure and Organization

- Import `defineQuery` and `groq` from `next-sanity` at the top of query files
- Export queries as constants using the `defineQuery` function
- Organize queries by content type (blogs, pages, products, etc.)
- Group related queries together

## Fragment Reuse

- Define common projection fragments at the top of the file
- Use string interpolation to include fragments in queries
- Ensure fragments are composable and focused on specific use cases

## Query Parameters

- Use `$` for parameters (e.g., `$slug`, `$locale`, `$id`)
- Handle localization with consistent patterns (e.g., `${localeMatch}`)
- Use `select()` for conditional logic within queries
- Define default parameters using `coalesce()`

## Response Types

- Export TypeScript interfaces for query responses when needed
- Use descriptive types that match the query structure
- Follow the pattern: `export type GetAllMainPageTranslationsQueryResponse = string[];`

## Best Practices

- Use explicit filtering (`_type == "x"`) rather than implicit type checking
- Prefer projection over returning entire documents
- Use `order()` for explicit sorting rather than relying on document order
- Check for defined fields (`defined(field)`) before accessing them
- Use conditional projections for optional fields
- Add pagination parameters (`[$start...$end]`) for list queries

## Code Style

- Use template literals for query strings
- Indent nested query structures for readability
- Keep related query parts together
- Maintain consistent whitespace and indentation
- Use comments to explain complex query logic

## Basic Schema Structure

For TypeScript files, always import the necessary Sanity types:

```typescript
import {defineField, defineType, defineArrayMember} from 'sanity'
```

Always use `defineField` on every field and `defineType` throughout the whole type. Only import `defineArrayMember` if needed:

```typescript
export default defineType({
  name: "hero-primary",
  title: "Hero Primary",
  type: "object",
  fields: [title, description, links, image],
  components: { preview: ModulePreview },
  preview: {
    select: {
      title: "title",
    },
    prepare({ title }) {
      return {
        title: toPlainText(title ?? []),
        subtitle: "Hero Primary",
        media: DashboardIcon,
      };
    },
  },
});
```